# Table of Contents

Use Microsoft Word's automatic Table of Contents feature after opening the document. Heading styles have been applied throughout this specification.

# 1. Introduction

## 1.1 Purpose

This document defines the complete functional requirements, non-functional requirements, system architecture, data model, API design, user workflows, security requirements, validation rules, testing strategy, deployment approach, and implementation constraints for the Smart Lecture Portal.

The document is intentionally written as an implementation baseline. An AI coding assistant should treat it as the source of truth for the first release and should not invent additional user roles, major modules, database entities, or workflows without explicit approval.

## 1.2 Product Vision

The Smart Lecture Portal is a web-based academic management and learning-support platform that connects lecturers and students. It centralizes course information, learning materials, assignments, submissions, attendance, marks, announcements, notifications, and academic reporting in one system.

## 1.3 Scope

The system has exactly two application roles:

Student: consumes learning resources, submits academic work, views academic information, and receives course communication.

Lecturer: manages assigned courses, publishes learning resources, creates and grades assignments, manages attendance and marks, and communicates with enrolled students.

There is no administrator dashboard in Version 1.0. Initial system configuration such as creation of accounts, courses, or academic structures is considered outside the application scope unless explicitly added in a future version.

## 1.4 Objectives

Provide secure role-based access for students and lecturers.

Centralize course materials and academic activities.

Allow lecturers to manage assignments, submissions, attendance, marks, and announcements.

Allow students to access learning resources, submit work, monitor attendance, and view marks.

Automate calculations such as attendance percentages and assignment/course totals where configured.

Provide useful dashboards and reports without requiring manual spreadsheet processing.

Maintain an auditable record of important academic actions.

Provide a responsive and maintainable architecture suitable for a final-year software engineering project.

# 2. Product Scope and Boundaries

## 2.1 In Scope

| **Module** | **Included Capabilities** |
| --- | --- |
| Authentication | Login, logout, password reset/change, session/token handling, role-based authorization |
| Student Dashboard | Overview of courses, assignments, attendance, marks, announcements and notifications |
| Lecturer Dashboard | Overview of assigned courses, pending grading, attendance, submissions, announcements and performance |
| Course Management | View/manage assigned courses, course details, enrollment visibility |
| Materials | Upload, list, view/download, update metadata and delete course materials |
| Assignments | Create, publish, update, close, grade and provide feedback |
| Submissions | Student upload/submission, submission status, lecturer review, grading and feedback |
| Attendance | Create lecture sessions, mark students, edit attendance with audit information, view summaries |
| Marks | Create assessment records, enter/update marks, calculate totals where configured, publish marks |
| Announcements | Create and display course announcements |
| Notifications | In-app notifications for important events |
| Timetable | Display relevant scheduled classes; lecturer view for assigned teaching sessions |
| Reports | Course-level attendance, marks, assignment and submission summaries |
| Profiles | View/update allowed profile fields and change password |
| Search/Filtering | Search and filter courses, materials, assignments, students and records within authorized scope |

## 2.2 Out of Scope for Version 1.0

Administrator role/dashboard.

University-wide student admission or registration.

Tuition/fee/payment processing.

Payroll and lecturer HR management.

Library management.

Hostel/accommodation management.

Examination timetable management at institution level.

Biometric attendance.

Facial recognition.

AI-generated grading or AI-generated academic decisions.

Public social networking.

Real-time video conferencing/class streaming.

Native Android/iOS apps.

Multi-university tenant management.

## 2.3 Future Enhancements

QR-code attendance.

Email/SMS/push notifications.

Online quizzes and question banks.

Discussion forums.

Calendar integration.

Advanced analytics and early-warning dashboards.

Native mobile application.

Optional AI features subject to separate requirements, privacy review and academic approval.

