## 3.1 Authorization Principle

Every protected API operation must verify both authentication and authorization. A valid login is not sufficient: the backend must confirm that the authenticated user owns the resource or has lecturer access to the relevant course. Frontend route guards are for user experience; backend authorization is mandatory for security.

# 4. Functional Requirements

## 4.1 Authentication and Account Management

| **ID** | **Requirement** |
| --- | --- |
| FR-AUTH-01 | The system shall allow a registered user to log in using their configured credentials. |
| FR-AUTH-02 | The system shall identify the user's role as Student or Lecturer after authentication. |
| FR-AUTH-03 | The system shall deny access to protected resources when the user is not authenticated. |
| FR-AUTH-04 | The system shall enforce role-based access controls on protected backend endpoints. |
| FR-AUTH-05 | The system shall provide logout and invalidate/expire the relevant authentication session or token. |
| FR-AUTH-06 | The system shall provide password reset/change flows using the selected authentication provider. |
| FR-AUTH-07 | The system shall never store plaintext passwords in application tables. |
| FR-AUTH-08 | The system shall provide appropriate authentication error messages without exposing sensitive information. |

## 4.2 Student

| **ID** | **Requirement** |
| --- | --- |
| FR-STU-01 | Student shall view a dashboard containing relevant courses, upcoming assignments, attendance summary, recent marks, announcements and notifications. |
| FR-STU-02 | Student shall view courses in which they are enrolled. |
| FR-STU-03 | Student shall view course details and lecturer information within authorized scope. |
| FR-STU-04 | Student shall view and download available course materials. |
| FR-STU-05 | Student shall view assignment instructions, deadline, total marks and status. |
| FR-STU-06 | Student shall upload an assignment submission before the applicable deadline. |
| FR-STU-07 | Student shall see whether a submission is submitted, late, graded, or returned for revision when such status is configured. |
| FR-STU-08 | Student shall view marks and lecturer feedback that have been released to the student. |
| FR-STU-09 | Student shall view attendance history and calculated attendance percentage for enrolled courses. |
| FR-STU-10 | Student shall view course announcements and relevant notifications. |
| FR-STU-11 | Student shall view the timetable relevant to their courses. |
| FR-STU-12 | Student shall update permitted profile fields and change password. |

## 4.3 Lecturer

| **ID** | **Requirement** |
| --- | --- |
| FR-LEC-01 | Lecturer shall view a dashboard containing assigned courses, pending submissions, upcoming deadlines, attendance and performance summaries. |
| FR-LEC-02 | Lecturer shall view only courses assigned to the authenticated lecturer. |
| FR-LEC-03 | Lecturer shall view students enrolled in assigned courses. |
| FR-LEC-04 | Lecturer shall upload, update metadata for, and delete course materials within assigned courses. |
| FR-LEC-05 | Lecturer shall create assignments for assigned courses. |
| FR-LEC-06 | Lecturer shall configure assignment title, instructions, deadline, maximum marks, publication status and optional attachment. |
| FR-LEC-07 | Lecturer shall view and download authorized student submissions. |
| FR-LEC-08 | Lecturer shall grade submissions and optionally provide feedback. |
| FR-LEC-09 | Lecturer shall create lecture attendance sessions for assigned courses. |
| FR-LEC-10 | Lecturer shall mark and correct attendance for enrolled students subject to audit rules. |
| FR-LEC-11 | Lecturer shall create assessment components and enter/update marks for enrolled students. |
| FR-LEC-12 | Lecturer shall publish or unpublish marks where the workflow requires release control. |
| FR-LEC-13 | Lecturer shall create, edit and publish course announcements. |
| FR-LEC-14 | Lecturer shall view course-level attendance, marks and assignment reports. |
| FR-LEC-15 | Lecturer shall view the timetable for assigned teaching sessions. |

## 4.4 Courses and Enrollment

| **ID** | **Requirement** |
| --- | --- |
| FR-COURSE-01 | The system shall store course code, course name, description, credit hours, academic period and status. |
| FR-COURSE-02 | Students shall only see courses for which an enrollment record exists. |
| FR-COURSE-03 | Lecturers shall only manage courses to which they are assigned. |
| FR-COURSE-04 | The system shall prevent duplicate enrollment for the same student and course offering. |
| FR-COURSE-05 | The system shall support course status such as active, archived or inactive. |

## 4.5 Materials

| **ID** | **Requirement** |
| --- | --- |
| FR-MAT-01 | Lecturer shall upload supported material files to an assigned course. |
| FR-MAT-02 | Each material shall have title, description/category, course, uploader, file reference, creation date and visibility status. |
| FR-MAT-03 | Students shall only access materials belonging to their enrolled courses. |
| FR-MAT-04 | The system shall validate allowed file types and file size. |
| FR-MAT-05 | Deletion of a material shall also handle the associated storage object according to retention rules. |

## 4.6 Assignments and Submissions

| **ID** | **Requirement** |
| --- | --- |
| FR-ASG-01 | Lecturer shall create draft assignments before publication. |
| FR-ASG-02 | Published assignments shall become visible to enrolled students. |
| FR-ASG-03 | The system shall validate that a deadline is logically valid. |
| FR-ASG-04 | Student shall be able to submit an allowed file or configured response before the deadline. |
| FR-ASG-05 | The system shall record submission timestamp and status. |
| FR-ASG-06 | The system shall prevent unauthorized students from submitting to an assignment. |
| FR-ASG-07 | The system shall support a configured late-submission policy; default Version 1.0 policy is to block submissions after the deadline unless the lecturer enables late submissions. |
| FR-ASG-08 | Lecturer shall be able to grade a submission only within their assigned course. |
| FR-ASG-09 | Grade shall not exceed the assignment maximum mark. |
| FR-ASG-10 | Student shall see released grades and feedback. |

## 4.7 Attendance

| **ID** | **Requirement** |
| --- | --- |
| FR-ATT-01 | Lecturer shall create an attendance session with course, date, start/end time and optional topic. |
| FR-ATT-02 | The system shall generate attendance records for enrolled students or otherwise provide a controlled marking interface. |
| FR-ATT-03 | Lecturer shall mark attendance as Present, Absent, Late or Excused if these statuses are enabled. |
| FR-ATT-04 | Student shall view their attendance history but shall not edit it. |
| FR-ATT-05 | The system shall calculate attendance percentage from applicable sessions. |
| FR-ATT-06 | The system shall prevent duplicate attendance sessions for the same course/time according to configured uniqueness rules. |

## 4.8 Marks

| **ID** | **Requirement** |
| --- | --- |
| FR-MARK-01 | Lecturer shall create assessment components such as CAT, assignment, practical or exam for an assigned course. |
| FR-MARK-02 | Each assessment shall have a maximum mark and optional weight. |
| FR-MARK-03 | Lecturer shall enter and update student marks within valid ranges. |
| FR-MARK-04 | The system shall calculate totals/weighted results according to the configured assessment scheme. |
| FR-MARK-05 | The system shall support a draft/unpublished state where marks should not yet be visible to students. |
| FR-MARK-06 | Students shall view only their own released marks. |
| FR-MARK-07 | The system shall record who changed a mark and when for auditability. |

## 4.9 Announcements and Notifications

| **ID** | **Requirement** |
| --- | --- |
| FR-NOT-01 | Lecturer shall create announcements for assigned courses. |
| FR-NOT-02 | Students enrolled in the relevant course shall be able to view published announcements. |
| FR-NOT-03 | The system shall generate in-app notifications for configured events such as new assignments, released marks, new materials and announcements. |
| FR-NOT-04 | Users shall be able to mark notifications as read. |

## 4.10 Timetable

| **ID** | **Requirement** |
| --- | --- |
| FR-TIME-01 | The system shall store scheduled teaching sessions with course, date/day, start time, end time, room/location and optional recurrence metadata. |
| FR-TIME-02 | Students shall view timetable entries for enrolled courses. |
| FR-TIME-03 | Lecturers shall view timetable entries for assigned courses. |

## 4.11 Reports

| **ID** | **Requirement** |
| --- | --- |
| FR-REP-01 | Lecturer shall view course attendance summaries. |
| FR-REP-02 | Lecturer shall view assignment submission summaries. |
| FR-REP-03 | Lecturer shall view assessment/marks summaries. |
| FR-REP-04 | The system shall provide student-level and course-level filtering where authorized. |
| FR-REP-05 | Reports shall not expose data outside the requesting user's authorization scope. |

# 5. Core User Workflows

## 5.1 Login

Open login page

Enter credentials

Authenticate

Resolve user role

Load role-specific dashboard

Record security-relevant login event where supported

## 5.2 Student Assignment Submission

Student opens course

Opens assignment

Reads instructions/deadline

Uploads file

System validates file and deadline

System stores submission

System records timestamp/status

Student receives confirmation

## 5.3 Lecturer Grading

Lecturer opens course

Opens assignment

Views submissions

Opens/downloads submission

Enters mark and feedback

System validates mark

Lecturer saves grade

Grade becomes visible only according to release policy

## 5.4 Attendance

Lecturer opens course

Creates attendance session

System identifies enrolled students

Lecturer marks status

System validates and saves records

Student later views attendance history and percentage

## 5.5 Course Material Upload

Lecturer opens assigned course

Selects Materials

Chooses file

Enters title/description

System validates file type/size

File is stored

Metadata is saved

Material becomes visible to authorized students

## 5.6 Marks Entry

Lecturer selects assessment

System loads enrolled students

Lecturer enters marks

System validates ranges

System saves marks

Totals are recalculated

Lecturer publishes when ready

Students see released results

# 6. Non-Functional Requirements

| **ID** | **Category** | **Requirement** | **Priority** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| NFR-SEC-01 | Security | All protected backend endpoints shall require authentication and authorization. | High |
| NFR-SEC-02 | Security | Passwords shall be handled by a trusted authentication provider; plaintext passwords shall not be stored. | High |
| NFR-SEC-03 | Security | File access shall use authorization-aware storage policies or controlled signed URLs. | High |
| NFR-SEC-04 | Security | User input shall be validated server-side and client-side. | High |
| NFR-SEC-05 | Security | The application shall avoid leaking stack traces, secrets, tokens or sensitive database details to clients. | High |
| NFR-SEC-06 | Security | Authorization checks shall prevent IDOR-style access to other users' records. | High |
| NFR-PERF-01 | Performance | Normal dashboard/API interactions should target sub-2-second response time under the expected project load, excluding large file transfer. | Medium |
| NFR-PERF-02 | Performance | List endpoints shall support pagination/filtering rather than loading unbounded datasets. | High |
| NFR-REL-01 | Reliability | Database writes for related records shall be transactional where consistency requires it. | High |
| NFR-REL-02 | Reliability | The system shall show clear recoverable errors and not silently discard user actions. | High |
| NFR-USE-01 | Usability | The UI shall be responsive and usable on desktop, tablet and mobile screen sizes. | High |
| NFR-USE-02 | Usability | Forms shall provide validation messages close to the relevant field. | High |
| NFR-USE-03 | Usability | Destructive actions shall require confirmation where appropriate. | Medium |
| NFR-MAIN-01 | Maintainability | Frontend and backend shall be modular and organized by feature/domain. | High |
| NFR-MAIN-02 | Maintainability | API contracts and environment variables shall be documented. | High |
| NFR-MAIN-03 | Maintainability | Core business logic shall be covered by automated tests. | High |
| NFR-SCAL-01 | Scalability | The architecture shall allow additional courses/users without redesigning core domain entities. | Medium |
| NFR-COMP-01 | Compatibility | The web application shall support current versions of major Chromium-based browsers and Firefox/Edge equivalents. | Medium |
| NFR-A11Y-01 | Accessibility | Interactive controls shall have labels, keyboard focus states and sufficient semantic structure. | Medium |

# 7. Technical Design

## 7.1 Recommended Technology Stack

| **Layer** | **Technology** | **Purpose** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Frontend | React + Vite | Component-based responsive web UI |
| Styling | CSS Modules or organized CSS; optional UI library | Maintainable responsive styling |
| Routing | React Router | Client-side route management |
| State/Data | React state + TanStack Query or equivalent | Server state, caching and async operations |
| Backend | FastAPI + Python | REST API and business logic |
| Validation | Pydantic | Request/response validation |
| Database | Supabase PostgreSQL | Relational persistent data |
| Authentication | Supabase Auth | Identity and session management |
| File Storage | Supabase Storage | Materials and submission files |
| API Documentation | FastAPI OpenAPI/Swagger | Interactive API documentation |
| Testing | Pytest + FastAPI TestClient; Vitest/React Testing Library | Backend/frontend tests |
| Version Control | Git + GitHub | Source control and collaboration |
| Deployment | Any compatible frontend host + FastAPI host + Supabase | Production deployment |

## 7.2 High-Level Architecture

Browser
   |
   | HTTPS
   v
React Frontend
   |
   | REST/JSON + authenticated requests
   v
FastAPI Backend
   |
   +--> Authentication/session verification
   |
   +--> Authorization / business rules
   |
   +--> PostgreSQL (Supabase)
   |
   +--> Supabase Storage
   |
   +--> Notification/event logic

Supabase Auth <--> User identity
Supabase PostgreSQL <--> Application data
Supabase Storage <--> Materials/submissions

## 7.3 Architectural Principles

Keep business rules on the backend; do not trust frontend validation.

Use resource ownership and course membership checks on every protected resource.

Keep API routes thin and place reusable business logic in service/domain modules.

Use database constraints for critical uniqueness and integrity rules.

Separate storage objects from database metadata.

Use environment variables for secrets and deployment-specific configuration.

Return consistent JSON error structures from the API.

Avoid direct database access from the browser for protected business operations; route business operations through FastAPI.

