# 9. Database Design

The following relational model is the baseline. Exact Supabase-generated auth tables are not duplicated in the application schema. The application profile table should reference the authentication user ID.

| **Table** | **Core Columns** | **Purpose** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| profiles | id (PK/auth user id), role, full_name, email, phone, avatar_url, created_at, updated_at | One profile per authenticated user |
| students | id (PK/FK profiles.id), registration_number, program, year_of_study, status | Student-specific profile data |
| lecturers | id (PK/FK profiles.id), staff_number, department, title, status | Lecturer-specific profile data |
| courses | id, course_code, course_name, description, credit_hours, academic_year, semester, status, created_at, updated_at | Course offering |
| course_lecturers | id, course_id FK, lecturer_id FK, assigned_at | Lecturer-to-course assignment |
| course_enrollments | id, course_id FK, student_id FK, enrolled_at, status | Student enrollment |
| materials | id, course_id FK, title, description, storage_path, file_name, mime_type, file_size, uploaded_by FK, published, created_at, updated_at | Course learning resources |
| assignments | id, course_id FK, title, description, instructions, due_at, max_marks, allow_late, published, attachment_path, created_by FK, created_at, updated_at | Assignment definitions |
| submissions | id, assignment_id FK, student_id FK, storage_path, file_name, file_size, submitted_at, status, mark, feedback, graded_by FK, graded_at, updated_at | Student submissions |
| attendance_sessions | id, course_id FK, session_date, start_time, end_time, topic, created_by FK, created_at | Lecture attendance session |
| attendance_records | id, session_id FK, student_id FK, status, marked_at, marked_by FK, note | Per-student attendance |
| assessments | id, course_id FK, name, type, max_marks, weight, published, created_by FK, created_at, updated_at | Assessment component |
| assessment_marks | id, assessment_id FK, student_id FK, mark, feedback, entered_by FK, entered_at, updated_at | Student mark per assessment |
| announcements | id, course_id FK, title, body, published, published_at, created_by FK, created_at, updated_at | Course communication |
| notifications | id, user_id FK, type, title, message, link, is_read, created_at, read_at | In-app notifications |
| timetable_entries | id, course_id FK, day_of_week/date, start_time, end_time, room, notes, created_at, updated_at | Scheduled teaching sessions |
| audit_logs | id, actor_user_id FK, action, entity_type, entity_id, old_value/json, new_value/json, created_at | Important change history |

## 9.1 Key Relationships

profiles 1---1 students
profiles 1---1 lecturers

courses 1---* course_lecturers *---1 lecturers
courses 1---* course_enrollments *---1 students

courses 1---* materials
courses 1---* assignments
assignments 1---* submissions *---1 students

courses 1---* attendance_sessions
attendance_sessions 1---* attendance_records *---1 students

courses 1---* assessments
assessments 1---* assessment_marks *---1 students

courses 1---* announcements
profiles 1---* notifications
courses 1---* timetable_entries

## 9.2 Database Integrity Rules

profiles.role must be one of: student, lecturer.

A student must not have duplicate registration_number.

A lecturer must not have duplicate staff_number.

course_code should be unique per course offering according to the chosen academic-period policy.

course_enrollments should have a unique (course_id, student_id) constraint.

course_lecturers should have a unique (course_id, lecturer_id) constraint.

attendance_records should have a unique (session_id, student_id) constraint.

assessment_marks should have a unique (assessment_id, student_id) constraint.

Marks must be between 0 and max_marks.

Assignment max_marks must be greater than zero.

Attendance status must use an approved enum/value set.

Foreign keys should use deliberate delete behavior; do not cascade-delete academic records without explicit policy.

# 10. REST API Design

The API should be versioned from the start, for example /api/v1. Exact route names may be refined during implementation, but the following contract should remain the baseline.

| **Module** | **Method + Endpoint** | **Purpose** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Auth | POST /api/v1/auth/login | Authenticate |
| Auth | POST /api/v1/auth/logout | Logout/session termination |
| Auth | POST /api/v1/auth/password/change | Change password |
| Profile | GET /api/v1/me | Current user profile |
| Profile | PATCH /api/v1/me | Update allowed profile fields |
| Courses | GET /api/v1/courses | List authorized courses |
| Courses | GET /api/v1/courses/{course_id} | Course details |
| Courses | GET /api/v1/courses/{course_id}/students | List enrolled students for lecturer |
| Materials | GET /api/v1/courses/{course_id}/materials | List materials |
| Materials | POST /api/v1/courses/{course_id}/materials | Create/upload material metadata |
| Materials | PATCH /api/v1/materials/{material_id} | Update material |
| Materials | DELETE /api/v1/materials/{material_id} | Delete material |
| Assignments | GET /api/v1/courses/{course_id}/assignments | List assignments |
| Assignments | POST /api/v1/courses/{course_id}/assignments | Create assignment |
| Assignments | GET /api/v1/assignments/{assignment_id} | Assignment details |
| Assignments | PATCH /api/v1/assignments/{assignment_id} | Update assignment |
| Assignments | POST /api/v1/assignments/{assignment_id}/submissions | Submit assignment |
| Submissions | GET /api/v1/assignments/{assignment_id}/submissions | Lecturer list submissions |
| Submissions | PATCH /api/v1/submissions/{submission_id}/grade | Grade submission |
| Attendance | POST /api/v1/courses/{course_id}/attendance/sessions | Create session |
| Attendance | GET /api/v1/courses/{course_id}/attendance/sessions | List sessions |
| Attendance | POST /api/v1/attendance/sessions/{session_id}/records | Save attendance records |
| Attendance | GET /api/v1/courses/{course_id}/attendance/me | Student attendance |
| Marks | POST /api/v1/courses/{course_id}/assessments | Create assessment |
| Marks | GET /api/v1/courses/{course_id}/assessments | List assessments |
| Marks | PUT /api/v1/assessments/{assessment_id}/marks | Bulk/upsert marks |
| Marks | GET /api/v1/courses/{course_id}/marks/me | Student marks |
| Announcements | GET /api/v1/courses/{course_id}/announcements | List announcements |
| Announcements | POST /api/v1/courses/{course_id}/announcements | Create announcement |
| Notifications | GET /api/v1/notifications | List notifications |
| Notifications | PATCH /api/v1/notifications/{id}/read | Mark notification read |
| Timetable | GET /api/v1/timetable | Get authorized timetable |
| Reports | GET /api/v1/courses/{course_id}/reports/attendance | Attendance report |
| Reports | GET /api/v1/courses/{course_id}/reports/performance | Performance report |

## 10.1 API Conventions

Use JSON for normal request/response bodies.

Use multipart/form-data for file upload endpoints.

Use ISO 8601 timestamps in UTC or a documented timezone strategy; display localized times in the UI.

Use consistent HTTP status codes: 200/201 for success, 400 for validation, 401 for unauthenticated, 403 for unauthorized, 404 for not found, 409 for conflict, 422 for schema validation where applicable, and 500 only for unexpected server errors.

Return a consistent error shape such as {code, message, details} without exposing internal stack traces.

Paginate potentially large collections.

Document every endpoint with OpenAPI schemas and authorization requirements.

