| REST | Representational State Transfer API style |
| CRUD | Create, Read, Update, Delete |
| SRS | Software Requirements Specification |
| API | Application Programming Interface |
| JWT | JSON Web Token, if used by the selected authentication architecture |
| RLS | Row Level Security, particularly relevant to Supabase/PostgreSQL |
| MVP | Minimum Viable Product |
| IDOR | Insecure Direct Object Reference; an authorization vulnerability |

# Appendix C — Final Implementation Principle

The Smart Lecture Portal should be built as a reliable academic management and learning-support system first. Features should be added because they solve a defined academic workflow, not simply because they are technically interesting. The first successful release should prioritize correctness, security, authorization, maintainability and demonstrable end-to-end workflows.

